                    },
                    "message": "I had the exact same issue which manifested in one of my other change\nhttps://jenkins.openbmc.org/job/ci-repository/137478/console\n\nAlso had a fix which looked almost same. Will comment."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I've made a much more targeted fix here:\n\n    remote:   https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/sdbusplus/+/91364 exception: handle sd_bus_error ownership properly\n    \nI'll leave this commit open in case you want to continue to enhance the test cases but I don't think the changes in `bus` and `message` are necessary."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/bus.hpp",
                    "line": 355,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: The documentation for `SdBusError` still says that it will become the owner of the error.\n\n```\n108     /** Becomes the owner of the error */\n109     SdBusError(sd_bus_error* error, const char* prefix,\n110                SdBusInterface* intf = &sdbus_impl);\n```\n\nTherefore in my fix the `SdBusError` constructor frees the error passed as argument.\n\n```\n--- a/src/exception.cpp\n+++ b/src/exception.cpp\n@@ -56,6 +56,10 @@ SdBusError::SdBusError(sd_bus_error* error_in, const char* prefix,\n {\n     intf->sd_bus_error_copy(&error, error_in);\n \n+    // idempotent on unset and already free'd errors\n+    // https://www.man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/sd_bus_error.3.html\n+    intf->sd_bus_error_free(error_in);\n+\n     populateMessage(std::string(prefix));\n }\n```\n\nWith that alternative the code becomes more compact and not necessary anymore to \nhave a local variable, can directly throw it in the error path.\n\nWhat do you think, can we do it that way or did i overlooked something ?\n\nIf we solve it like PS1, do we need to update the comment for the `SdBusError` constructor?"
                }
            ],
